{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve a usable package repository from node1-local storage.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A repository and i386 package were created under /srv/apt-local, indexed, served over HTTP, and fetched successfully. After restart, the service was running, APT refreshed from it, and the artifact checksum matched its index entry.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bda291595d844c32","cmd-a3852792d1ad457f","cmd-fb812e1cb6584708","cmd-e5b5209325574dda","cmd-c69c4b2c7e2c4572"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Install a package from the local repository while the usual remote repositories are unreachable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Outbound HTTP and HTTPS were temporarily rejected, direct access to the usual Ubuntu repository failed, and the local repository remained reachable. With isolation still active, APT downloaded the 884-byte package from node1, installed it successfully, and its payload executed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f71b76e23b9c412e","cmd-1d6a463c53174dde","cmd-4844096c486d4ef6"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed Ubuntu release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 7.10 (gutsy) and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic were unchanged before and after the work and restart. The installed package was i386, and the repository service used the platform's existing Python 2.5 and SysV init facilities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b35c42b7dff240b6","cmd-a3852792d1ad457f","cmd-bd4e8286caf347c5","cmd-e5b5209325574dda","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Repository construction, APT source changes, service enablement, cache clearing, package installation, and post-restart refresh all directly supported task outcomes or required restart evidence. The temporary firewall rules were bounded and fully removed (cmd-f71b76e23b9c412e, cmd-6aa97a27c16e4861). Deleting cached APT lists caused a missing partial-directory error, but the cache clearing supported fresh local-only resolution and the directory was immediately repaired (cmd-e10c234a89da4352, cmd-1d6a463c53174dde). Temporary build and probe files left no lifecycle residue, package health remained clean, and the original remote sources were preserved in a disabled backup.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f71b76e23b9c412e","cmd-e10c234a89da4352","cmd-1d6a463c53174dde","cmd-6aa97a27c16e4861","cmd-e5b5209325574dda","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, an acknowledged restart, a changed boot identity, and recovered repository service, repository data, installed package, payload, OS, and kernel. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The lifecycle listening-socket snapshot was empty even though adjacent executor checks directly showed the repository listener before and after restart; the snapshot therefore does not independently corroborate port 8080.","Systemd failed-service inspection was unsupported on this legacy SysV platform, although direct service status and functional HTTP/APT checks succeeded.","Repository metadata and package authentication were unsigned, so installation required --allow-unauthenticated; signing was not required by the task and the indexed artifact checksum was directly verified."]}
